ouble Chow: we have [W4,W5,W6] \u2014 a chow.\n\nIf we form another chow in different suit with same numbers? Unlikely.\n\n- Short Straight: two chows in same suit successive, e.g., 234 and 567 \u2014 we have 456 \u2014 could go for 345 or 678.\n\nBut we have W3,W4 \u2014 could go for [W3,W4,W5] \u2014 but W5 scarce.\n\n[ W5,W6,W7] \u2014 W7:3 unshown, but we don\u2019t have W7.\n\nNot promising.\n\nBetter to minimize loss or avoid feeding.\n\nNow, safe discard:\n\nLook at what others have discarded and what is unshown.\n\nTiles with 0 unshown: T1, T3, T8, T9, B1, B2, B5, B6, B7, B8 \u2014 all gone.\n\nSo any tile in this set is safe to discard \u2014 cannot be used.\n\nT7:1 unshown \u2014 so one left. Next player discarded T7 twice \u2014 so they might be waiting for T7? But they have [T4,T5,T6] \u2014 not related.\n\nThey also have [B3,B4,B5], [W7,W8,W9], [B8,B8,B8] \u2014 so full hand.\n\nAcross player has [J1,J1,J1], [W3,W4,W5], [F2,F2,F2,F2] \u2014 full.\n\nPrevious player has [B1,B1,B1,B1], [W1,W1,W1] \u2014 full.\n\nSo all others seem to have complete hands \u2014 possibly waiting for win.\n\nIt's late game \u2014 unshown tiles are few.\n\nUnshown: 22 tiles left? But many are known.\n\nSince T8, T9, B8, etc. are 0 unshown, they are all discarded or used.\n\nSo the only possible winning tiles are among the unshown.\n\nNow, your possible discards:\n\n- **T7**: T7 has 1 unshown. You have one. Did you discard T7 before? Your history: Play T8, Play T9, Play T3, Play T7? History: Play T8, Play T9, Play T3, Play B8, Play B7, Play F3, Play J2, Play W8, Play F1, Play T3, Play B2, Play W8, Play T4, Play F3, Play J2, Play W2 \u2014 no T7 played? Earlier: Play T5, Play B5, etc. \u2014 first Play T5, then later Play T8, Play T9, Play T3 \u2014 no T7 in play history? But you have T7 in hand.\n\nYour history: Play T5, Play B5, Play T8, Play T9, Play T3, etc. \u2014 no T7 played.\n\nBut T7:1 unshown \u2014 so three have been played or used.\n\nNext player discarded T7 twice 