nly valid actions are Chi W3 and Pass. Although Chi W3 is listed, my hand contains W3 and W4, but lacks W2 or W5 (W5 is already used in an exposed meld) to form a legal Chow with a discarded W3. Forming [W2,W3,W4] requires W2 (unavailable), and [W3,W4,W5] requires W5 which is already melded. Thus, Chi W3 is not realistically formable. Passing is the only safe and legal choice.\n\nReason: Attempting Chi W3 would require tiles I do not possess or cannot reuse, making it an invalid move despite being listed. Therefore, I must pass.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
